  "id": "unbiased",
  "term": "unbiased",
  "definition": "In research methods, unbiased means free from a systematic tendency to favor some outcomes over others. A sample is unbiased when each member of the population has the same chance of selection, and an estimator is unbiased when it does not consistently overestimate or underestimate the value it is meant to estimate.",
